// CRYPT SHIFT — DEAD MAN'S GULCH — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CRYPT SHIFT as a gothic spaghetti western in the Morricone manner — the ghost town at
// midnight, a cowboy's ghost in the crypt. A game alternate of crypt, selectable from the dev
// menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// The tune is crypt.js's, note for note, and so is its harmony; the hook goes to a twangy
// BARITONE electric (FRPP-6 bridge pickup, an octave under the theme) through an amp
// tremolo and a spring tank, and a WHISTLE answers it two octaves up — one melody passed
// between two players. NYLON rasgueado (all down-strokes: a thumb-bass trot, 3+3+2
// flamenco strums, four-finger rolls, a galloping strum), a second nylon on down-up
// sixteenths (alternate strum) under the climb, BANJO forward rolls, MANDOLIN tremolo, a
// SLIDE guitar howling; wood-block hooves, whip cracks with a canyon echo, an anvil, timpani
// in A and E, a tolling bell and the wind. The showdown is a mariachi TRUMPET with a second
// trumpet in thirds and sixths under it.
// 
// Under the baritone the guitar hand moves with the tune: Am lifts to Asus2 and F opens to
// Fmaj7#11 where the tune lands on B, so no C ever rubs it. Shapes (low E to high e):
// Am x02210, Asus2 x02200, Fmaj7 1x3210, Fmaj7#11 1x3200, E 022100, E7 020100, Dm9 xx3210, Dm xx0231, Cmaj7 x32000, C x32010, G 320003, Bm x24x32.
// 
//   1–4    INTRO        midnight: bell, wind, the whistle on the intro line, mandolin tremolo, slide howls, hooves arriving
//   5–8    A            the RIDER: baritone hook (5–6), whistle answers (7–8); nylon trot, hooves, crypt bass; anvil, whip
//   9–12   A            again, the banjo rolling and the shaker in
//   13–16  B            whistle on the B phrase (13–14), baritone answers (15–16); flamenco 3+3+2 strums, mandolin; snare + timpani roll into the eclipse
//   17–24  GHOST CHOIR  the eclipse: no gallop; choir on the middle-eight tune, slide howls the replies, mandolin tremolo, baritone roots, bells
//   25–28  A            the RETURN: baritone + whistle two octaves apart; nylon gallop strum, banjo rolls, anvil on 4, crash
//   29–32  C            the CLIMB: whistle + choir an octave apart; nylon down-up sixteenths (alternate strum); kick on the beat; timpani + snare roll
//   33–36  A            SHOWDOWN: trumpet hook + second trumpet in thirds/sixths, baritone 8vb, choir pad; nylon gallop, banjo, snare + anvil on 2 & 4, tambourine
//   37–40  D            the descent (Am G F E) on the trumpets, a snare fill into 41
//   41–44  A            the last hook with EVERYTHING — whistle 2 octaves up, choir pedal; bar 44 is the draw: band stops, trumpets alone, slide howl, the shot
//   45–48  OUTRO        DUST: wind, bell, baritone alone on the outro phrase, whistle echo, single strums, hooves trotting off, slide howl, the gallop back into bar 5
// 
// WEATHER SYNC: the crypt eclipse runs on the heard song beat (CRYPT_WEATHER_TIMING, a
// 192-beat cycle). This song keeps the live theme's 98 BPM and its 48 bars — one cycle —
// with the Ghost Choir on bars 17–24 (beats 64–96): the clouds gather on bar 16's snare roll,
// the gallop stops for the choir, and comes back at 25 as they clear. The loop is bars 5–48,
// no boundary inside 16–28. The generator asserts it.
// 
// Mix: levelled by soloed LUFS section by section (_remix-bounce --lanes --range): the tune
// (baritone, whistle, choir, trumpet) at one level in every section, the showdown 1.5 dB
// hotter; nylon ~7 under, banjo and mandolin ~9–10, hooves ~9, bass ~2–3, the second
// trumpet ~6, the slide ~3–4 under the choir. Bright high shelves on the tunes and guitars,
// a sine under the bass. mbCompN, then a trailing gain of -2.4 dB: −21.0 LUFS integrated.
// 
// 48 bars at 98, 118 s. Written by work/local/_crypt-remix-dead-mans-gulch.mjs
// through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; it self-checks chord tones on the beats, no semitone
// clashes, one note per string, the alternate strum's parity, the loop wrap and the
// landmarks; re-running it rewrites this file.
